namespace trion.propositional:
    primitive proposed approximation counterexample relation
    primitive added assumption, approximation, assumption, auxiliary variable, candidate scope
    primitive checked problem, constant, conversion stage, missing capability, negative polarity
    primitive original slot order, query condition truth, query scope, required capability, result
    primitive violated conversion precondition, witness

    section "Exact Boolean conversion":
        cite FOUNDATION
        A target term means a Boolean constant, a signed slot, a conjunction, or a disjunction.
        A target problem means a conjunction of target terms.
        An empty conjunction is true.
        A target valuation uses the original declaration slots.

        ref [PROP-QUERY-CONDITION]

        [PROP-NNF]
        The propositional translator shall push negations to constants and slots.
        The propositional translator shall exchange conjunction and disjunction under negative polarity.
        The propositional translator shall invert a constant or signed slot under negative polarity.

        [PROP-EXACT]
        The propositional translator shall preserve the truth of the query condition at every valuation.
        The propositional translator shall add no assumption.
        The propositional translator shall add no auxiliary variable.
        The propositional translator shall use the original slot order for a witness.

        [PROP-CAPABILITIES]
        The propositional translator shall derive required capabilities from the checked problem.
        The propositional translator shall report a missing capability as unsupported.
        The propositional translator shall report a violated conversion precondition.
        The propositional translator shall preserve the checked document.

        [PROP-TRANSLATION-TRACE]
        The propositional translator shall record the conversion stages and target problem.

    source PROP-APPROXIMATION:
        title "Counterexample contracts for future extensions"
        locator "urn:trion:propositional:counterexample-contracts"
        kind citation
        quote RULES """
Exact translation represents exactly the original counterexamples.
Overapproximation contains every original counterexample and can add candidates.
Underapproximation covers only a subset of the original counterexamples.
A verified absence of candidates implies absence of original counterexamples for exact translation and overapproximation.
Underapproximation with no candidate leaves the original query undecided.
A recovered candidate must satisfy the original counterexample condition.
A search bound is part of a bounded proposition. It does not establish the unbounded proposition.
A conclusion under extra assumptions remains conditional unless those assumptions follow from the original premises.
"""

    section "Scope of translation":
        cite FOUNDATION
        [PROP-COUNTEREXAMPLE-CONTRACT]
        The propositional maintainer shall record the counterexample relation of a proposed approximation.
            cite PROP-APPROXIMATION#RULES

        [PROP-EXACT-ONLY]
        The propositional translator shall reject approximation.
        The propositional translator shall reject added assumptions.
        If the candidate scope differs from the query scope, then the propositional checker shall reject the result.
